Parity with the web source (verified by reading it end-to-end):
  - parseScheduleSignals  -> ChargingScheduleSignals.parse
       (ScheduledChargingMode / Pending / StartTime / DepartureTime / ChargeLimitSoc)
  - modeLabel / modeBadgeVariant -> projection.modeLabel / modeTone
       (StartAt,DepartBy=success · Off=neutral · unknown/nil=warning; raw fallback)
  - hasScheduleData, timelineItems (start/departure/targetLimit, same order/tones)
  - compact branch (chargeLimit% headline + "Charge Limit") and EmptyState fallback
  - full branch: mode StatusPill(dot) + Pending badge + Timeline OR "No scheduled
    times set"; tall detail row (Current Level / Status = Charging|Not Charging)
  - states reproduced: loading, empty, error(retry), stale chip, offline chip,
    loaded compact/full/tall (+cached-error indicator)

Architecture (matches the repo's established facade pattern, VehicleSettingsModel):
  - @Observable @MainActor model bound to an injected ChargingScheduleDataSource
    (the P1/S8 vehicle+signals holder conforms to it). NO I/O in the view.
  - Pure, Shared-free ChargingScheduleProjection + ChargingScheduleDisplay routing
    => every state branch is unit-testable without the KMP framework.
  - Shared component library only (TSCard, TSStatusPill, TSBadge, TSTimeline,
    TSEmptyState, TSQueryError, TSSkeleton, TSMetric*) + design tokens; no raw
    Tailwind ports, no direct chart/map libs (none needed for this surface).
  - i18n: every key resolves through the P1/S10 catalog (no English literals):
    translation.widget.chargingSchedule.* (14), translation.widget.charging,
    translation.widget.notCharging, widget.freshness.* , translation.common.refresh
    -> all confirmed present in apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings.
  - a11y: refresh button labelled (translation.common.refresh); freshness chip
    label+value (widget.freshness.accessibility); metric/detail combine elements.
  - Telemetry: model emits view.opened once with surface slug "ChargingScheduleWidget".

